alDefinitionsCompared%27%2C%20%27semanticObligationsChecked%27%2C%20%27unprovedMeaningEquivalenceRejected%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recursiveDefinitionsRequest%27%2C%20definitionSource%2C%20%27ontology-and-taxonomy-entry-points%27%2C%20%27ontology-and-taxonomy%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-LIBRARY-ENTRYPOINT%27%2C%20%27separate%20ontology%20library%20entry%20point%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20expose%20a%20separate%20ontology%20entry%20point%20for%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%20in%20the%20global%20space%2C%20including%20concepts%20unused%20by%20any%20language%20grammar.%20Their%20definitions%20and%20links%20remain%20available%20without%20caller%20grammar%20registration.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyEntryPointAvailable%27%2C%20%27grammarUnusedConceptsAvailable%27%2C%20%27ontologyDefinitionsAndRelationsInspectable%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-LIBRARY-ENTRYPOINT%27%2C%20%27separate%20taxonomy%20library%20entry%20point%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Both%20packages%20expose%20a%20separate%20taxonomy%20entry%20point%20for%20classification%20and%20explicitly%20declared%20subsumption%20links%20over%20the%20global%20concept%20space%2C%20including%20concepts%20unused%20by%20grammars.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27taxonomyEntryPointAvailable%27%2C%20%27classificationAndSubsumptionInspectable%27%2C%20%27grammarUnusedTaxonomyConceptsAvailable%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-MEMBERSHIP%27%2C%20%27concept%20membership%20in%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%20or%20both%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20concept%20can%20occur%20in%20the%20ontology%2C%20taxonomy%20or%20both%20through%20the%20same%20global%20identity.%20Grammar%20reachability%20never%20removes%20a%20concept%2C%20and%20both%20entry%20points%20retain%20its%20recursive%20formal%20definition%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27sharedOntologyTaxonomyIdentity%27%2C%20%27membershipIndependentOfGrammarReachability%27%2C%20%27definitionsAndProvenanceRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-TAXONOMY-RELATION-DISTINCTION%27%2C%20%27distinction%20between%20general%20relations%20and%20classification%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20ontology%20represents%20concepts%2C%20relationships%20and%20formal%20axioms%3B%20the%20taxonomy%20represents%20classification%20or%20declared%20subsumption.%20An%20arbitrary%20associative%20relation%20does%20not%20become%20a%20classification%20edge%2C%20and%20the%20chosen%20hierarchy%20semantics%20remain%20explicit%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27ontologyAndTaxonomyRolesDistinct%27%2C%20%27arbitraryRelationsDoNotImplyClassification%27%2C%20%27hierarchySemanticsExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ONTOLOGY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20ontology%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20ontology%20can%20have%20several%20independently%20selectable%20roots%2C%20each%20represented%20as%20an%20explicit%20link%20in%20the%20global%20space.%20A%20root%20may%20also%20be%20a%20type%20only%20when%20its%20model%20declares%20that%20role%3B%20root%20selection%20and%20traversal%20retain%20identity%20and%20provenance.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleOntologyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27ontologyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-TAXONOMY-MULTIPLE-LINK-ROOTS%27%2C%20%27multiple%20explicit%20taxonomy%20root%20links%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20taxonomy%20can%20have%20several%20explicitly%20represented%20root%20links%20and%20multiple%20classification%20entry%20points.%20A%20root%20type%20role%20is%20declared%20by%20the%20selected%20model%20rather%20than%20inferred%20from%20being%20a%20root%2C%20and%20classification%20traversal%20preserves%20its%20declared%20semantics.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27multipleTaxonomyRootsSelectable%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27taxonomyRootTypeRoleExplicit%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27linksFoundationRequest%27%2C%20linksSource%2C%20%27links-as-fundamental-entities-and-relationships%27%2C%20%27links-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-UNIVERSAL-REPRESENTATION%27%2C%20%27links%20as%20the%20fundamental%20representation%20of%20concepts%2C%20entities%20and%20relationships%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20represented%20concept%2C%20entity%2C%20relationship%2C%20root%20and%20formal%20definition%20is%20fundamentally%20a%20link%20or%20composition%20of%20links%20in%20the%20same%20network.%20Independent%20host%20objects%20or%20hidden%20side%20tables%20cannot%20substitute%20for%20the%20common%20representation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27conceptsEntitiesRelationshipsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27rootsAndDefinitionsAreLinks%27%2C%20%27noHiddenEntityRepresentation%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-SELF-LOOP-VERTEX%27%2C%20%27vertex%20represented%20by%20a%20self-referencing%20link%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20selected%20links%20model%20can%20represent%20a%20vertex%20as%20a%20link%20whose%20beginning%20and%20end%20reference%20that%20same%20link.%20Its%20identity%2C%20self-reference%20and%20selected%20model%20are%20explicit%20and%20survive%20serialization%20and%20reload.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27selfLoopVertexRepresentable%27%2C%20%27selfReferencingEndpointsPreserved%27%2C%20%27vertexModelAndIdentityRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-MULTIPLE-ROLES%27%2C%20%27one%20link%20as%20relationship%2C%20concept%20and%20entity%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20same%20link%20can%20carry%20relationship%2C%20concept%20and%20entity%20roles%20without%20replacing%20its%20identity%20with%20disconnected%20host%20representations.%20Role%20declarations%20and%20multiple%20root%20selections%20remain%20inspectable%20links.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27linkIdentitySharedAcrossRoles%27%2C%20%27rolesAreExplicitLinks%27%2C%20%27multipleRootRolesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-RECURSIVE-COMPOSITION%27%2C%20%27recursive%20compositional%20links%20across%20representation%20levels%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Links%20can%20reference%20and%20compose%20other%20links%20recursively%20across%20representation%20levels%2C%20preserving%20the%20reusable%20structural%20motif%2C%20shared%20references%20and%20explicit%20cycles.%20This%20compositional%20model%20does%20not%20itself%20establish%20a%20mathematical%20fractal%20dimension%20or%20eliminate%20logical%20paradoxes.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27recursiveLinkCompositionPreserved%27%2C%20%27sharedMotifAndCyclesExplicit%27%2C%20%27noUnprovedConsistencyInference%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-OPTIONAL-TYPE-ROOT%27%2C%20%27declared%20type%20roots%20without%20a%20universal%20self-typing%20axiom%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27A%20model%20may%20declare%20a%20root%20link%20to%20be%20a%20type.%20The%20representation%20does%20not%20infer%20a%20universal%20Type%3AType%20axiom%20or%20a%20universal%20proof%20logic%20from%20links%2C%20self-loops%2C%20recursion%20or%20root%20membership%3B%20foundation%20premises%20remain%20explicit%20and%20selectable.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27rootTypeRolesDeclared%27%2C%20%27noImplicitUniversalSelfTyping%27%2C%20%27selectedFoundationPremisesPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27linksFoundationRequest%27%2C%20linksSource%2C%20%27links-as-fundamental-entities-and-relationships%27%2C%20%27links-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-LINK-FOUNDATION-PHYSICAL-ANALOGY%27%2C%20%27recorded%20wave%20and%20fractal%20motivation%20with%20an%20explicit%20epistemic%20boundary%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20user%20wave%2C%20particle%20and%20fractal%20analogy%20is%20preserved%20verbatim%20as%20motivation%20and%20a%20hypothesis.%20Documentation%20and%20formal%20models%20do%20not%20report%20those%20physical%20propositions%2C%20universal%20self-similarity%20or%20freedom%20from%20contradictions%20as%20established%20facts%20or%20consistency%20proofs.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27physicalAnalogyCapturedVerbatim%27%2C%20%27physicalPropositionsMarkedAsHypotheses%27%2C%20%27noAnalogyPresentedAsConsistencyProof%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27recordConversationRequest%27%2C%20recordingSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27conversation-contract%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONVERSATION-VERBATIM-REGISTER%27%2C%20%27immutable%20hashed%20capture%20of%20every%20requirement-bearing%20conversation%20message%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20requirement-bearing%20conversation%20message%20is%20captured%20verbatim%20with%20its%20content%20hash%20and%20explicit%20capture%20provenance%2C%20registered%20as%20a%20source%20and%20linked%20to%20atomic%20obligations.%20New%20messages%20append%20captures%20rather%20than%20overwriting%20earlier%20requests.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27conversationMessagesCapturedVerbatim%27%2C%20%27captureHashesVerified%27%2C%20%27allConversationObligationsMapped%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONVERSATION-CRITICAL-DELIVERY%27%2C%20%27critical%20classification%20of%20all%20conversation%20and%20inherited%20obligations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20conversation%20requirement%20and%20every%20inherited%20ledger%20obligation%20is%20critical%20and%20blocks%20a%20full-scope%20delivery%20or%20release-completion%20claim%20while%20it%20lacks%20required%20exact-commit%20evidence.%20Existing%20source%2C%20scope%2C%20assertions%2C%20fixtures%2C%20runtimes%20and%20checkpoint%20execution%20order%20remain%20intact.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27allRequirementsCritical%27%2C%20%27unverifiedRowsBlockFullScopeDelivery%27%2C%20%27inheritedScopeAndCheckpointsPreserved%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27associativeFoundationRequest%27%2C%20stackSource%2C%20%27associative-stack-and-theoretical-foundation%27%2C%20%27associative-foundation%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-STACK-PINNED-SOURCE-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27pinned%20audit%20of%20the%20referenced%20associative%20technology%20stack%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20project%20audit%20reads%20the%20referenced%20formal-ai%20associative%20technology%20stack%20at%20a%20recorded%20immutable%20revision%20and%20records%20its%20content%20hash%2C%20providers%20and%20dependency-role%20boundaries.%20A%20moving%20main%20URL%20or%20a%20provider%20name%20alone%20does%20not%20establish%20adoption.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27associativeStackSourceReadAndPinned%27%2C%20%27stackContentHashRecorded%27%2C%20%27providerRolesClassified%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSOCIATIVE-STACK-PROJECT-WIDE-USE%27%2C%20%27associative%20stack%20adoption%20across%20the%20entire%20project%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27An%20executable%20project-wide%20audit%20covers%20both%20packages%2C%20code%2C%20grammars%2C%20translation%2C%20tools%2C%20documentation%20and%20dependencies%20against%20the%20relevant%20associative%20stack%20obligations.%20Direct%20runtime%20providers%2C%20compatibility%20or%20theoretical%20alignment%20and%20development%20tools%20are%20distinguished%3B%20unrelated%20formal-ai%20dependencies%20are%20not%20blindly%20introduced.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27entireProjectStackUsageAudited%27%2C%20%27actualCodeAndDependenciesTraced%27%2C%20%27runtimeCompatibilityAndDevelopmentRolesDistinct%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-THEORY-FOUNDATION-PINNED-SOURCE-AUDIT%27%2C%20%27pinned%20philosophical%20and%20theoretical%20meta-theory%20foundation%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27The%20meta-theory%20source%20is%20read%20at%20an%20immutable%20revision%20with%20archived%20releases%20and%20drafts%20identified%20separately.%20Adopted%20definitions%2C%20assumptions%20and%20provenance%20are%20recorded%20explicitly%3B%20a%20repository%20citation%20alone%20is%20insufficient%20as%20a%20theoretical%20foundation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27metaTheorySourceReadAndPinned%27%2C%20%27archivesAnd